### 1. Kurzgesagt (@kurzgesagt)

Munich animation studio, Steve Taylor VO, 10–16 min.

**Steal:** first-line stakes in “you” (“You will never leave the solar system.”); “you” throughout; sources in the description; Shorts that exist to pull the long.

**Do not clone:** birb / flat-vector house style; 8s logo intro; 60–90s shop / pin reads; Interlingua joke; merch as the outro. Orbit already forbids shop reads.

Recent longs often skip the old logo sting and cold-open on the picture. Latest long *Why Humanity Will Never Leave The Solar System* (`Cyl3X88KEgg`) pre-rolls a shop ad — **do not copy that close**.

### 2. SEA (@SEA / @sea)

**This handle is Sam Anderson**, UK space-doc channel (SEA Media Ltd), channel ID `UCG9ShGbASoiwHwFcLcAh9EA`. About: “I make chilled out videos about all things space-related. I don't use AI or do promotional content.” **Not** Garena, **not** SEA Today News, **not** `@sea_space`.

Typical long 26–32 min. Opens on a 10s logo (black → static → “SEA” card), VO starts ~10s. Ends “I thank you very much for watching and I bid you goodnight. SEA signing out.”

**Steal:** journey / scale structure (Earth → outward); superlative titles; Shorts → full film; no promo reads; listed sources; a **named** goodbye.

**Do not clone:** anonymous 10s logo void; “bid you goodnight / signing out” verbatim; faceless channel with no Ben and no Orbit.

### 3. History of the Universe (@historyoftheuniverse)

David Kelly, Horizon / Cosmos-style 45–160 min essays, named scientist writers, Ettore Mazza thumbs.

Opens picture-first in 1–3s (scene, not logo). Latest ToE (`nPLKfvr_y4E`) flashes a 2s “written, narrated and created by humans” card then the sky.

**Steal:** scene-open before the thesis; chaptered long-form; named writer / credits as trust; one-line like / sub / comment; sources in description or pinned comment.

**Do not clone:** 1–2 hour Horizon pastiche; painted-thumb style; “You've been watching the entire history of…”; no face, no Orbit; mid-roll software sponsors.

